{"prompt": "Write a poem about how I am missing my classes. The poem must have 4 sections marked with SECTION X. Finish the poem with this exact phrase: \"Can I get my money back for the classes I missed?\"", "response": "SECTION 1\nThe calendar turns, a silent thief,\nStealing hours from my waking life.\nThe lecture hall sits empty, cold,\nA story left half-told, unrolled.\nI watch the clock with heavy eyes,\nAs knowledge slips through empty skies.\n\nSECTION 2\nThe notes remain blank, the pages bare,\nWith no one there to whisper care.\nThe professor\u2019s voice, a distant echo,\nLeaves me in a quiet, lonely becho.\nI trace the lines of what I missed,\nA shadow cast by time\u2019s swift list.\n\nSECTION 3\nThe syllabus gathers dust and gray,\nThe lessons fade, the words decay.\nI sit alone in the empty room,\nChasing a phantom, chasing a gloom.\nThe investment feels like a loss,\nA hollow space, a silent cross.\n\nSECTION 4\nThe semester ends, the final bell,\nRings out for me, a hollow spell.\nI look at the receipt, the cost,\nOf all the time I paid the most.\nCan I get my money back for the classes I missed?"}
