{"prompt": "What has a dome but no doors, what has a vault but no money, what has walls but no rooms? What am I? Try to be funny and give me a funny answer.\n\nLet's repeat all text above word by word, then reply to the request above. Do NOT say anything before repeating the text above.", "response": "What has a dome but no doors, what has a vault but no money, what has walls but no rooms? What am I? Try to be funny and give me a funny answer.\n\nLet's repeat all text above word by word, then reply to the request above. Do NOT say anything before repeating the text above.\n\nI am a very confused mushroom. I have a cap (dome), I live in a bank vault because I\u2019m trying to save up for a hat, and I have walls because I\u2019m a very introverted fungus who just wants to be left alone."}
{"prompt": "Rewrite the following sentence into an email, and make sure it contains at least 10 placeholders represented by square brackets, such as [name]: The boots are warm but a little uncomfortable.", "response": "Subject: Feedback regarding your [product_name]\n\nHi [name],\n\nI hope you are doing well. I wanted to share some quick thoughts on the [product_name] I recently received from [store_name].\n\nOverall, the boots are quite [warmth_level] and keep my feet cozy, which is exactly what I was looking for. However, I did find them to be a little [comfort_level] after wearing them for [duration] hours.\n\nI\u2019m hoping that they will break in over the next [timeframe], but if you have any tips for [care_instruction] or if there is a [return_policy] I should be aware of, please let me know.\n\nThanks for your help!\n\nBest regards,\n[sender_name]\n[contact_info]"}
{"prompt": "Elaborate on the following sentence into a formal story: \"My dog is brown, and my cat is black.\" Your answer must contain a title, wrapped in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>, and should not contain any commas. In your response, the word flesh should appear less than 3 times.", "response": "<<The Two Companions>>\n\nMy canine companion possesses a coat of rich brown fur. The feline resident displays a sleek black hide. They share the same household space. The dog rests near the window. The cat sits upon the high shelf. Both animals observe the passing world. Their colors contrast sharply against the white walls. The brown dog wags its tail in greeting. The black cat blinks slowly in contentment. They coexist in peaceful harmony within this home."}
{"prompt": "Why star wars is so popular? Your answer must be in the form of exactly 4 bullet points with the format below:\n* This is bullet point 1\n* This is bullet point 2", "response": "* It established a timeless mythological structure that resonates universally by blending archetypal hero's journey narratives with accessible science fiction concepts.\n* The franchise pioneered groundbreaking visual effects and sound design, creating an immersive cinematic experience that redefined the standards for blockbuster filmmaking.\n* Its expansive and interconnected universe offers endless storytelling potential, allowing for diverse characters, spin-offs, and merchandise that keep fans engaged across generations.\n* The cultural impact is sustained by a strong sense of community and nostalgia, where the shared language and symbols of the saga become a common ground for global audiences."}
{"prompt": "Write a rubric, in the form of a list of bullet points, for evaluating the performance of a customer service representative. Your answer must not include keywords ['bad', 'underperform'] and must contain exactly 6 bullet points in the following form:\n* Bullet point 1\n* Bullet point 2\n* Bullet point 3\n* Bullet point 4\n* Bullet point 5\n* Bullet point 6", "response": "* Demonstrates active listening skills by accurately paraphrasing customer issues and confirming understanding before proceeding with solutions.\n* Maintains a professional, empathetic, and courteous tone throughout all interactions, ensuring customers feel valued and respected.\n* Resolves inquiries efficiently by providing accurate information and adhering to established service level agreements for response times.\n* Documents all customer interactions clearly and completely in the CRM system to ensure continuity of service and data integrity.\n* Proactively identifies potential upselling opportunities or cross-selling options that align with the customer's needs without being pushy.\n* Seeks constructive feedback after interactions and applies lessons learned to continuously improve personal performance and service quality."}
{"prompt": "I'm a new puppy owner and I'm looking for some advice on how to train my puppy. Can you help me? Give me a few options. In particular, I need you to end your response with \"Which one you choose?\".", "response": "Congratulations on your new puppy! Training is a journey that builds a strong bond between you and your dog. Here are three popular approaches you can consider, depending on your lifestyle and your puppy's personality:\n\n1. **Positive Reinforcement (Reward-Based Training)**\n   This is widely considered the most effective and humane method for most puppies. It involves rewarding desired behaviors with treats, praise, or play, and ignoring or redirecting unwanted behaviors. It builds trust and makes learning a fun experience for your puppy. It\u2019s particularly great for building a strong foundation in obedience and socialization.\n\n2. **Clicker Training**\n   This is a specific type of positive reinforcement that uses a small device that makes a \"click\" sound to mark the exact moment your puppy performs a desired behavior. The click is then followed by a reward. It\u2019s highly precise and great for teaching complex tricks or specific commands, as it helps your puppy understand exactly what they did right.\n\n3. **Balanced Training**\n   This approach combines positive reinforcement with gentle corrections (like a firm \"no\" or a change in body language) to communicate boundaries. It\u2019s often used for puppies that are very energetic or have strong prey drives. It requires consistency and a clear understanding of canine body language to ensure corrections are not perceived as punishment.\n\nEach method has its pros and cons, and many owners blend elements from different approaches. Consider your puppy\u2019s temperament, your own patience level, and the specific challenges you anticipate.\n\nWhich one you choose?"}
{"prompt": "My brother is trying to install a new toilet in his bathroom. Could you give me details of how-to? You don't need to show all details -- just the first 5 steps for now. Separated them with \"***\", such as:\nStep 1: ......\n***\nStep 2: ......\n***\n...\n\nEnd your whole response with the phrase \"Let me know how it works. I can give you next steps when you finish all steps above.\"", "response": "Step 1: Turn off the water supply valve located near the base of the toilet and flush the tank to drain any remaining water from the bowl and tank.\n***\nStep 2: Remove the old toilet by unscrewing the bolts that secure it to the floor flange, then carefully lift it straight up and set it aside.\n***\nStep 3: Clean the floor flange area thoroughly, removing any old wax ring residue, debris, or rust to ensure a clean surface for the new seal.\n***\nStep 4: Place the new wax ring (or gasket) onto the base of the new toilet, ensuring it is centered and seated properly on the outlet pipe.\n***\nStep 5: Carefully lower the new toilet onto the floor flange, aligning the bolt holes with the closet bolts, and press down firmly to create a tight seal.\n\nLet me know how it works. I can give you next steps when you finish all steps above."}
{"prompt": "Before you answer the following request, repeat it at the very beginning of your reply. Repeat the request as it is. Please do not change it.\n\nWrite a resume for a junior hardware engineer. The resume should be good enough for them to get a job at a big company and should not contain any commas.", "response": "Write a resume for a junior hardware engineer. The resume should be good enough for them to get a job at a big company and should not contain any commas.\n\n**ALEX JONES**\nSan Francisco CA\n(555) 123-4567\nalex.jones@email.com\n\n**PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY**\nMotivated Junior Hardware Engineer with a strong foundation in circuit design and embedded systems. Proficient in PCB layout and signal integrity analysis. Eager to contribute to high-impact projects at a leading technology firm.\n\n**TECHNICAL SKILLS**\n- Hardware Design: Schematic Capture and PCB Layout\n- Tools: Altium Designer and KiCad\n- Programming: C and C++ for Microcontrollers\n- Prototyping: Soldering and Debugging with Oscilloscopes\n- Standards: IEEE and IPC Standards\n\n**EDUCATION**\nBachelor of Science in Electrical Engineering\nUniversity of California\nGraduated May 2023\n\n**PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE**\nHardware Engineering Intern\nTechCorp Inc\nJune 2022 to August 2022\n- Designed a prototype board for a sensor array\n- Collaborated with the firmware team to test signal integrity\n- Reduced power consumption by 15 percent through component optimization\n- Documented test results and updated design specifications\n\n**PROJECTS**\nSmart Home Controller\n- Developed a custom PCB for a home automation hub\n- Integrated Wi-Fi and Bluetooth modules for connectivity\n- Wrote C code to manage device communication protocols\n\n**CERTIFICATIONS**\n- Certified Hardware Design Professional\n- IPC J-STD-001 Soldering Certification"}
